WEBVTT

00:08.110 --> 00:11.550
My first impression was of a normal boy.

00:18.400 --> 00:24.220
But he wasn't like the immature 
boys that I disliked.

01:58.230 --> 01:59.770
Princess Kathyln?!

02:00.060 --> 02:01.520
And Prince Curtis?!

02:02.050 --> 02:07.070
#11 The King Celebrates.

02:06.330 --> 02:07.770
What's the meaning of this?

02:08.160 --> 02:11.930
Your Highness, my friends 
and I were enjoying a chat

02:11.930 --> 02:15.280
when that barbaric commoner 
attacked us for no reason!

02:15.600 --> 02:17.910
Of all the nerve. You were—

02:17.910 --> 02:19.910
We were doing nothing!

02:21.560 --> 02:23.850
Do you really think you 
could injure this dwarf

02:23.850 --> 02:26.670
and expect us to believe that excuse?

02:26.900 --> 02:28.170
Is that true?

02:28.170 --> 02:31.160
No, sir! It was in self defense!

02:31.590 --> 02:35.370
<i>It's such an obvious lie. 
How can my brother be so foolish?</i>

02:35.370 --> 02:37.180
What absolute idiocy.

02:37.400 --> 02:38.930
Arthur!

02:39.280 --> 02:43.120
How dare you speak to the 
prince of Sapin like that!

02:45.580 --> 02:50.260
I have to apologize. I tend to speak 
in a coarse fashion when I hear lies.

02:50.690 --> 02:54.270
<i>He's so small. Where is all 
this strength coming from?!</i>

02:54.270 --> 02:55.820
Now, now.

02:55.820 --> 02:59.240
Please forgive my nephew.

02:59.240 --> 03:02.830
He is simply trying to say that 
those other boys are lying.

03:02.830 --> 03:06.210
Mr. Helstea? What are you doing here?

03:06.210 --> 03:10.340
We came across that group 
bullying the other boy.

03:12.240 --> 03:14.840
You dare lie to me?

03:15.300 --> 03:16.480
Identify yourself.

03:19.300 --> 03:24.350
My name is Jamiel. I am the eldest son 
of the Trident family, Your Highness.

03:25.360 --> 03:26.850
The Tridents?

03:27.920 --> 03:30.360
<i>This has become complicated.</i>

03:30.570 --> 03:31.880
<i>The Tridents make</i>

03:31.880 --> 03:35.290
<i>significant donations to both Xyrus 
Academy and the royal family.</i>

03:35.290 --> 03:38.110
<i>If something were to 
happen to their heir...</i>

03:39.860 --> 03:41.470
Your acts of violence are—

03:41.470 --> 03:44.800
Given that nobody was seriously injured,

03:44.800 --> 03:49.090
if all involved agree to 
overlook what's happened...

03:49.090 --> 03:53.880
<i>Of course. Even royalty 
won't risk messing with me.</i>

03:54.350 --> 03:58.760
Uncle Vincent, you have one of those 
rolled letter communicators, right?

04:00.010 --> 04:02.090
I do, yes.

04:03.430 --> 04:04.520
Who are you contacting?

04:07.230 --> 04:09.160
Cynthia Goodsky.

04:09.780 --> 04:11.110
<i>Is this kid a moron?</i>

04:11.110 --> 04:14.780
<i>Does he really think the director of
 Xyrus Academy will answer?</i>

04:15.270 --> 04:17.100
Vincent.

04:17.100 --> 04:21.310
I can't say I appreciate you contacting 
me without any warning like this.

04:21.310 --> 04:23.160
It's Arthur Leywin, ma'am.

04:23.160 --> 04:28.660
Arthur! You, on the other hand, 
I'm always happy to hear from.

04:28.660 --> 04:30.730
How long has it been?

04:30.730 --> 04:33.420
<i>She sure changed her tune!</i>

04:33.420 --> 04:38.080
A student at the academy, 
Jamiel Trident, and his friends

04:38.080 --> 04:40.810
were bullying a dwarf because 
of their prejudice.

04:41.210 --> 04:44.180
I'd like you to expel them.

04:44.180 --> 04:49.050
This is what you called me about? 
And did you say Trident?

04:49.050 --> 04:51.060
I understand, 
but considering who's involved...

04:51.060 --> 04:55.190
<i>And there we go. That commoner might 
be familiar with the director,</i>

04:55.190 --> 04:58.590
<i>but that's nothing compared 
to the amount of money</i>

04:58.590 --> 05:00.950
<i>we've poured into the academy.</i>

05:01.260 --> 05:04.450
If you still want me to enroll...

05:04.450 --> 05:07.200
All right, they're expelled!

05:16.720 --> 05:19.720
Please forgive my earlier behavior.

05:19.430 --> 05:24.350
I should have been more firm in my response;
that was unbecoming of a prince.

05:24.680 --> 05:29.350
I should apologize as well.
My emotions got the better of me.

05:29.580 --> 05:34.910
Justifiably so. We must eliminate racial 
discrimination from the continent.

05:39.700 --> 05:43.760
Arthur, eh? He seems like a handful.

05:44.550 --> 05:47.080
I thought as much when 
I first met him, but...

05:47.080 --> 05:50.360
Hey, are you listening to me?

05:50.750 --> 05:51.620
Excuse me.

05:52.700 --> 05:56.000
Would you care to join 
me for tea sometime?

06:01.760 --> 06:02.760
Certainly.

06:05.310 --> 06:08.260
I'll see you at the academy then.

06:17.640 --> 06:22.030
What was that?! What happened to 
my cold-blooded, taciturn sister?!

06:24.020 --> 06:27.600
<i>There really is something 
different about him.</i>

06:30.890 --> 06:34.770
Humans, elves, and dwarves 
in attendance...

06:35.370 --> 06:39.880
I am Blaine Glayder, 
king of the Kingdom of Sapin.

06:40.310 --> 06:43.670
The kings and queens of your kingdoms

06:43.670 --> 06:46.430
have all gathered here 
on this momentous day.

06:47.130 --> 06:51.890
Are you all aware of the animosity 
between men and elves?

06:52.140 --> 06:56.540
Or how dwarves have been considered 
little more than business partners?

06:57.280 --> 07:01.090
I ask you to let the past be the past,
 cast aside your old prejudices,

07:01.090 --> 07:04.500
and look at things from a new perspective.

07:04.900 --> 07:07.950
Doing so will serve not only
 your own best interests,

07:07.950 --> 07:13.790
but those of your children, 
and the future of the entire continent!

07:20.630 --> 07:25.330
<i>The other continent is finally 
being revealed to the public.</i>

07:25.790 --> 07:31.110
<i>What I'm worried about is the 
fact that they've been able to</i>

07:31.110 --> 07:33.930
<i>camouflage mana beasts in 
order to surveil Dicathen.</i>

07:34.840 --> 07:41.470
<i>That would imply they 
either fear us or are hostile.</i>

07:41.470 --> 07:43.140
Is something wrong, Arthur?

07:45.630 --> 07:48.820
You seemed like your 
mind was somewhere else.

07:50.200 --> 07:51.870
I wouldn't say that.

07:53.220 --> 07:55.710
In discussions about the 
future of our continent,

07:55.710 --> 07:59.800
I have found myself in 
agreement with King Glayder.

08:00.380 --> 08:03.200
There are places within our home,
 the Dicathen Continent,

08:03.200 --> 08:06.910
where few have ever tread 
due to the danger.

08:08.020 --> 08:11.700
But suppose that even 
greater danger and mystery

08:11.700 --> 08:13.970
existed outside of our continent.

08:14.930 --> 08:19.100
We are here today, ladies and gentlemen,
 to officially announce...

08:19.500 --> 08:25.060
that we have evidence of another 
continent existing beyond Dicathen.

08:29.440 --> 08:35.300
We can confirm that they have 
attempted to make contact with us,

08:35.700 --> 08:42.210
but neither of our continents have the 
technology to make such a long journey.

08:42.520 --> 08:47.460
All of us are kin, in that we were 
born on the continent of Dicathen.

08:47.460 --> 08:50.550
I myself am proud of this fact,

08:50.550 --> 08:54.720
and would hope that future 
generations feel the same way.

08:55.130 --> 08:58.630
This marks the beginning 
of a new era for those of us

08:58.630 --> 09:01.980
who call this continent our home!

09:07.230 --> 09:10.340
There will surely be challenges 
in coordinating

09:10.340 --> 09:12.740
the three races and
 their respective kingdoms.

09:13.030 --> 09:14.510
As part of that,

09:14.510 --> 09:17.240
we would like to name six 
individuals and their new duties.

09:20.230 --> 09:24.520
They are representatives 
of their respective races,

09:24.520 --> 09:28.760
trusted by the royalty of each for 
their courage and intelligence.

09:29.280 --> 09:32.150
The six of them will work 
to ensure the safety and

09:32.150 --> 09:34.260
prosperity of their homelands,

09:34.260 --> 09:38.080
in a new era which we will 
all be able to enjoy.

09:38.460 --> 09:41.750
They will be collectively 
known as the Six Lances,

09:41.750 --> 09:46.900
and in time become known as 
symbols of our continent.

09:49.680 --> 09:51.170
Alea Triscan.

09:54.910 --> 09:56.410
Varay Aurae.

09:57.620 --> 09:59.280
Olfred Warend.

10:00.160 --> 10:01.660
Aya Grephin.

10:02.660 --> 10:04.570
Mica Earthborn.

10:05.420 --> 10:07.020
Bairon Wykes.

10:10.500 --> 10:12.420
Did he just say "Wykes"?

10:12.980 --> 10:14.680
As in Lucas' brother?

10:19.590 --> 10:25.440
To the Six Lances: you are to 
defend us all and seize glory.

10:25.440 --> 10:29.520
To all who train to become 
mages: with daily dedication,

10:29.520 --> 10:33.200
you may one day become 
one of the Six Lances!

10:33.510 --> 10:36.190
Because potential is limitless!

10:37.400 --> 10:41.790
<i>This was a day where I was 
confronted with reality.</i>

10:42.500 --> 10:44.210
<i>Lucas Wykes...</i>

10:45.040 --> 10:46.920
<i>Despite causing the death of his comrades,</i>

10:46.920 --> 10:50.710
<i>using his family's connections and authority,
he was cleared of wrongdoing.</i>

10:51.530 --> 10:55.580
<i>I had been warned that retribution 
against Lucas would be suicidal,</i>

10:55.580 --> 10:59.120
<i>and now I see that's due to his brother.</i>

10:59.780 --> 11:05.220
<i>A brother who is not simply a powerful 
mage, but now one of the Lances.</i>

11:10.330 --> 11:15.160
<i>I had more pressing matters to 
attend to than Lucas, anyway.</i>

11:15.530 --> 11:18.290
<i>Yay! Let's go, let's go!</i>

11:18.700 --> 11:20.530
You have to stay and watch my room.

11:24.360 --> 11:28.980
Uncle Vincent warned us about strangers 
sneaking in during the party.

11:28.980 --> 11:31.800
I don't want to put you in danger.

11:32.270 --> 11:36.550
Don't worry. I'll bring back
plenty of food.

11:36.550 --> 11:38.550
<i>Yay!</i>

11:41.710 --> 11:44.490
Welcome. Please, come inside.

11:45.270 --> 11:48.580
You'll want to ask him for a dance later.

11:48.580 --> 11:50.310
Mother...

11:52.260 --> 11:56.630
Y'know, I'm actually 
enrolling in Xyrus Academy.

11:56.630 --> 11:58.520
Maybe we could go out for tea sometime...

11:58.520 --> 11:59.320
Huh?

11:59.320 --> 12:03.720
I actually made this metal. 
If you'd like, I could...

12:04.720 --> 12:06.700
Your black hair is so lovely.

12:09.380 --> 12:11.650
<i>He reeks of desperation.</i>

12:12.300 --> 12:14.590
And now, tonight's guest of honor!

12:15.080 --> 12:16.590
Everybody get ready!

12:18.090 --> 12:21.850
What happened to a small 
party with just family?

12:27.100 --> 12:31.440
Happy birthday, Eleanor!

12:31.440 --> 12:33.180
Happy birthday!

12:45.080 --> 12:48.000
I'd like to thank you all for coming.

12:48.430 --> 12:53.470
I appreciate you celebrating 
my dear daughter's birthday with us!

12:54.330 --> 12:55.500
Dad...

12:55.500 --> 13:00.640
I've led a pretty charmed life, 
and now my greatest desire

13:00.640 --> 13:05.360
is to see my darling son and 
daughter dance together!

13:06.720 --> 13:09.290
I didn't know they were 
going to be dancing.

13:09.990 --> 13:11.770
When did they practice?

13:12.430 --> 13:14.190
They didn't!

13:14.190 --> 13:16.270
Damn it, Reynolds!

13:16.270 --> 13:20.030
No way! I don't even know how to dance!

13:20.540 --> 13:21.400
Eleanor.

13:23.580 --> 13:26.670
Would you give me the 
honor of this dance?

13:26.980 --> 13:31.160
Arthur... But I...

13:38.670 --> 13:40.920
Start the music!

13:54.560 --> 13:56.820
It sure looks like they practiced.

13:56.820 --> 13:58.320
But they didn't.

14:33.050 --> 14:35.320
<i>I didn't expect the high 
society dancing I learned</i>

14:35.320 --> 14:37.340
<i>in my past life to come in 
handy at a time like this.</i>

14:37.340 --> 14:39.340
That was amazing, Eleanor!

14:39.340 --> 14:41.860
That was such splendid 
dancing, it made me sick.

14:44.260 --> 14:46.360
Got a minute to talk?

14:48.040 --> 14:52.500
<i>I could really use a drink tonight, 
but I suppose juice will have to suffice.</i>

14:53.020 --> 14:54.700
You're a showy little bastard, aren't you?

14:54.700 --> 15:00.380
What can I do for the continent's 
premiere engineer tonight?

15:00.380 --> 15:02.880
Wonderful. He's sarcastic, too.

15:03.240 --> 15:07.250
I came to let you know that the 
adjusted design for your vessel

15:07.250 --> 15:10.640
was approved by the advisory committee 
and construction has begun.

15:11.210 --> 15:12.780
The advisory committee?

15:13.460 --> 15:16.260
It's a gathering where the royalty
 of Dicathen's three kingdoms

15:16.260 --> 15:20.270
can speak to each other on equal footing.

15:20.490 --> 15:25.400
Congratulations. I can only imagine 
the reward you got for its design.

15:25.400 --> 15:30.960
Money, fame, and authority are nothing 
more but a means to an end for me.

15:30.960 --> 15:32.450
What I really want is—

15:32.450 --> 15:33.410
Um, excuse me!

15:33.760 --> 15:35.640
You're Professor Gideon, right?

15:35.640 --> 15:37.260
We saw the news.

15:37.260 --> 15:39.420
You designed that massive boat...

15:38.420 --> 15:41.130
I'm a bit busy at the moment—

15:39.420 --> 15:42.200
I'm a huge fan of yours! It's really you!

15:41.590 --> 15:44.420
Hey, Arthur! I'm not done talking to you!

15:42.640 --> 15:46.340
<i>Fame certainly comes with its drawbacks.</i>

15:52.250 --> 15:54.180
Arthur!

16:01.830 --> 16:04.690
Thanks. I didn't know you were out here.

16:05.140 --> 16:07.840
I hear you've been really busy 
since joining the student council.

16:07.840 --> 16:09.950
Yeah. I just got here, in fact.

16:10.550 --> 16:12.450
It's been a while, Lilia.

16:12.450 --> 16:15.200
Yes. It really has.

16:16.190 --> 16:19.330
Were you always taller than me?

16:21.460 --> 16:25.080
From the boys who've been staring at you,

16:25.080 --> 16:27.000
I have to assume you're 
pretty popular at school.

16:28.620 --> 16:31.470
I don't have a boyfriend 
or anything, okay?!

16:31.990 --> 16:36.600
Besides, it's thanks to 
you that my life changed.

16:37.080 --> 16:38.690
Well, if you really feel that way...

16:39.350 --> 16:43.610
Any boyfriend you get has 
to get my seal of approval!

16:43.610 --> 16:47.360
I can be just as harsh as 
Uncle Vincent, you know.

16:48.830 --> 16:53.370
I guess so. You probably wouldn't...

16:54.240 --> 16:56.120
Pardon me, young lady.

16:56.390 --> 16:59.870
Do you mind if I borrow 
your friend for a moment?

17:00.120 --> 17:01.880
Professor Gideon?!

17:02.180 --> 17:03.880
Of course!

17:04.650 --> 17:06.830
I'll talk to you later, Arthur.

17:09.350 --> 17:12.630
See what I mean?
I'm a veritable celebrity.

17:12.630 --> 17:14.640
And so modest, to boot.

17:14.900 --> 17:17.750
I have to say, you're quite 
the little lady killer.

17:17.750 --> 17:20.140
That girl's fallen for you, you realize.

17:20.140 --> 17:21.140
I know.

17:21.480 --> 17:23.780
You seem to get along well enough,

17:23.780 --> 17:25.610
but you don't intend to things further?

17:25.610 --> 17:30.230
The way she feels about me has 
less to do with attraction

17:30.230 --> 17:33.410
and more to do with gratitude.

17:33.920 --> 17:38.540
She might not realize that yet, 
but she will in time.

17:38.540 --> 17:42.290
The way you sound so experienced at 
your age is absolutely infuriating.

17:42.540 --> 17:46.110
You didn't stop by to give me 
dating advice, did you?

17:46.110 --> 17:49.050
Oh, right. What I was trying to say is...

17:49.310 --> 17:53.280
I intend to use the money, fame, and 
authority that the committee provides me

17:53.280 --> 17:55.300
to obtain something in particular.

17:56.810 --> 17:58.560
Your knowledge!

18:05.630 --> 18:09.720
I already regret sharing the 
design for the steam engine.

18:10.810 --> 18:15.320
I don't want to divert this world from its 
natural path any more than I already have.

18:18.330 --> 18:21.830
Things had been going well enough on 
this continent without my intervention.

18:21.830 --> 18:26.330
Then you do have more ideas with 
the potential to change the world!

18:26.590 --> 18:28.600
Hell yeah!

18:27.560 --> 18:31.340
He only hears what he wants to, huh?

18:31.850 --> 18:33.040
Mr. Gideon.

18:34.060 --> 18:39.100
Let me be blunt: I have no intention of 
satisfying your selfish, personal curiosity.

18:40.010 --> 18:43.180
Well, you certainly know 
how to kill a buzz.

18:43.600 --> 18:46.600
In that case, how about a
give-and-take relationship?

18:48.350 --> 18:51.380
I won't ask for the kind of knowledge 
that can change the world,

18:51.380 --> 18:54.570
but I would appreciate you lending 
me your brain from time to time.

18:54.570 --> 18:58.710
In exchange, I'll provide 
you with anything you need.

18:58.710 --> 18:59.870
How's that sound?

19:02.630 --> 19:04.370
Do you accept?

19:10.230 --> 19:11.820
Consider it a deal.

19:17.000 --> 19:18.890
This seems lovely.

19:19.150 --> 19:21.150
Another dress?

19:25.680 --> 19:28.150
There's another present here.

19:30.650 --> 19:32.720
Who's it from?

19:37.110 --> 19:38.400
There's a letter.

19:39.690 --> 19:41.750
"Dear Eleanor."

19:41.750 --> 19:45.540
"I'm sure you're tired of all the 
dresses and tea sets you've received."

19:46.620 --> 19:48.040
It's a bow!

19:51.020 --> 19:53.130
And it's so beautiful!

19:53.130 --> 19:55.300
This design looks elvish.

19:56.100 --> 19:58.300
The letter isn't signed.

20:01.580 --> 20:03.500
<i>Could it really be...</i>

20:04.390 --> 20:08.080
Did you really wanna just leave 
the present without seeing anyone?

20:08.080 --> 20:12.320
I'd rather all of Arthur's 
attention be on his sister today.

20:12.320 --> 20:17.830
I totally get what you mean. Having to 
meet your crush's family takes courage.

20:17.830 --> 20:19.570
It's not like that!

20:19.570 --> 20:22.790
Then you didn't want any interruptions 
for your emotional reunion?

20:22.790 --> 20:24.990
Not that, either!

20:24.990 --> 20:26.080
Arthur and I...

20:26.960 --> 20:29.580
We'll see each other at 
the academy soon enough.

20:31.830 --> 20:34.960
Where's my present from 
my favorite big brother?

20:34.960 --> 20:38.660
Eleanor! You've received 
enough presents already.

20:45.960 --> 20:47.130
What are these?

20:47.130 --> 20:48.850
And there's something for me, too?

20:50.870 --> 20:52.610
A necklace!

20:52.610 --> 20:57.360
If you wear that, you'll be safe 
even when Dad and I aren't around.

20:57.670 --> 21:01.080
That's so lovely. Where do 
they sell necklaces like that?

21:01.080 --> 21:06.110
Unfortunately, they're the only two 
like them in the entire world.

21:06.520 --> 21:08.870
Happy birthday, Eleanor.

21:11.560 --> 21:14.880
<i>These are the people I care about.</i>
